{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p1-73e45bc0","text":"The user wants a shine effect that travels across the "Upload Photo" TEXT ONLY — clipped to the letter shapes. The classic technique: wrap the text in a span, apply `background: linear-gradient(...)` with `background-clip: text` and animate `background-position` from left to right. The text color comes from the gradient: base color + narrow bright highlight that moves across.

Key constraints:
- Text keeps existing font/size/weight/position/color (outside the highlight, text must retain normal existing color).
- No border/background/icon changes.
- Infinite loop, smooth, slow, slight pause between passes (e.g., shine travels over ~2.5s, then rests ~3s — implement with keyframe percentages: shine sweep during 0–40%, static rest 40–100%).
- No visible jump: base color at both 0% and 100% of the sweep, highlight fully off-screen at start/end.
