The screenshot confirms the fix: the full "Upload Photo" is visible — "Upload" in normal white, "Photo" fully rendered in the blue/cyan gradient with no letters missing.

**Done — the cut-off is fixed and "Photo" now runs a true seamless looping gradient.**

**Root cause of the clipping:** the previous version used `background-size: 200%` with **`background-repeat: no-repeat`** and animated the position from `0%` to `200%`. Past the 100% mark, a no-repeat layer slides entirely off the element — glyphs left with no background behind them render invisible under `text-fill-color: transparent`, so "Photo" appeared chopped mid-cycle (your screenshot caught such a frame).

**The fix:**
- `background-repeat: repeat` — the gradient layer now tiles, so **every glyph is covered at every instant** of the animation (verified: all sampled positions report `repeat`, coverage never breaks).
- The gradient itself is one periodic `blue → cyan → blue → cyan → blue` tile; the keyframes now animate `0% → 100%` of a 200% layer — exactly one tile width — so the loop is **mathematically seamless** (position at t=0 and t=5000ms are identical, verified), no cyan→blue jump, no reset flash.

**Verified live:**
- Full text "Upload Photo" always present — range probe shows the word's glyph rects intact and inside the button; `text-overflow` untouched; button 42px, width/position/border/background unchanged.
- The gradient physically travels: sampled positions `16% → 32% → 48% → 64% → 84%` across the cycle while the letters stay stationary.
- Colors only blue `rgb(47,127,209)` and cyan `rgb(34,184,212)` — clipped to the glyphs (`background-clip: text`), nothing outside the letters, no shine remnants (zero old-shine references in the file).
- "Upload" keeps its theme color (light `rgb(41,38,31)` / dark `rgb(242,243,241)`); "Photo" gradient identical in both themes.
- `prefers-reduced-motion` freezes the gradient statically; production build passes.

One robustness bonus fixed en route: the JSX word-split previously forced a "Photo" fallback for locales whose label doesn't end in "Photo" (e.g., Bengali "ছবি আপলোড করুন") — that would have appended a stray English word. The gradient span now only renders when the label actually ends with "Photo"; other locales show their plain label untouched.
