Done — every 7-day forecast card is now fully interactive, and the floating window's detail section follows the selection.

## How it works now

- **`selectedForecastDay` state** (index into `weather.forecast`, 0 = Today), initialized to 0 and reset to Today each time the modal opens — the initial appearance is unchanged.
- **All 7 cards are real `<button>`s** — the entire card is clickable (not just the text), with `cursor: pointer`, the pre-existing hover tint, a subtle 4% press-scale (`:active`), a keyboard focus ring, `aria-pressed` for accessibility, and `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` for clean mobile taps. Tapping Tomorrow/Mon/…/Fri immediately updates the details — same code path on mobile, layout untouched.
- **One selected at a time**: the highlight class moved from a hard-coded `--today` to `--selected`, so clicking another day un-highlights the previous one and highlights the new one using the exact same visual state Today had (green tint + leaf-colored day name).

## Real data only — derived per selected day

Every value comes from the day's actual Open-Meteo forecast object (`{ high, low, rain, wind, conditionKey }` already in `weather.forecast`):

| Section | Today selected | Future day selected |
|---|---|---|
| Big temperature | live current temp (unchanged default) | that day's forecast **high** |
| Condition + illustration | live current condition (unchanged) | that day's condition (translated label + icon) |
| Metric row | Feels-like, Humidity, Wind, Visibility (live) | **Low temp**, **max Wind** |
| Spraying advisory | shown (it's worded "…today") | hidden |

That gating is the honest edge-case handling: Open-Meteo's *daily* forecast block simply doesn't provide feels-like, humidity, or visibility for future days — so those tiles hide rather than show invented numbers, exactly per your requirement. Wind falls back gracefully (`sel?.wind`) if a value is ever missing. One new translation key (`weather.low`) was added in all 5 languages (EN/BN/HI/TE/TA).

## Smoothness & design

Switching days remounts only the two detail blocks (React `key`), playing a fast 240ms opacity fade — the modal shell never re-renders or jumps; the 7-day grid, glass, close button, and all styling are untouched.

## Verification

- Build passes; **lint 20 warnings / 0 errors** (baseline)
- All 9 structural checks verified against the **live transformed module** served by Vite (state init 0, reset-on-open, per-card `setSelectedForecastDay(i)`, button cards, `--selected` class, `aria-pressed`, real `sel.high/low/wind` wiring, Today-keeps-live-data, advisory-today-only)
- Live API probe confirmed the exact endpoint/fields the detail section reads return real 7-day values (e.g. tomorrow: 31.9°/26.1°, 84% rain, 8 km/h wind)
- Full interactive click-through wasn't possible in this preview partition (the modal lives inside the auth-gated shell and there's no session here) — one login in the preview and the cards are yours to tap; `git status` shows only the 3 intended files.
