Onboarding flow complete and verified. Build clean (~0.8s), lint at baseline **20 warnings / 0 errors**.

## What was built

**Flow (as specified):** Language → Auth (guests only, skippable) → Parcel count → Area+unit rows → Rice variety (fuzzy autocomplete) → Crop stage → "All set!" → dashboard. Back/Next preserve everything; "Skip for now" on every step; inline validation only (no `alert()`).

**New files**
- `supabase/migration_onboarding.sql` — `profiles` / `farms` / `land_parcels` with full RLS keyed to `auth.uid()`, `updated_at` triggers, and an auto-profile trigger on sign-up. **Needs one manual run in the Supabase SQL Editor** (I have no SQL access).
- `src/hooks/useOnboarding.jsx` — state provider; Supabase persistence with silent localStorage fallback if tables are absent, so nothing breaks before you run the migration.
- `src/components/onboarding/` — `OnboardingWizard` (auth-glass card, "Step X of N" bar), `OnboardingGate` (renders wizard instead of shell until done/skipped; returning users pass straight through), `GuestLanguageGate` (guests answer only language), `EmptyFarmNotice`.
- `src/lib/fuzzySearch.js` (prefix → substring → typo-tolerant subsequence, deterministic, over the single `riceVarieties` dataset) and `src/lib/onboardingService.js` (persistence layer).
- `src/data/cropStages.js` — the 8-stage rice vocabulary.

**Reused existing systems, nothing redesigned** — `AuthLayout`/`Auth.css` tokens for the wizard; `useLanguage` + `LANGUAGES` for the language step (pick applies live via `changeLanguage`); `ProtectedRoute`, `AuthProvider` patterns.

**Key behaviors verified live in preview:** Skip → guest → language-only gate; empty states on My Farm/Finance/Dashboard (hero hidden, no demo numbers) with working "Finish farm setup" CTA; full survey walk-through including typo query "psa 1121"→Pusa 1121; greeting name now real (`কৃষক` fallback, never "Anantā Maurya"); completed farm → My Farm renders real parcels (৬.৭ বিঘা, Bengali digits); reload skips the wizard. Skip ≠ complete (skipped users are re-prompted once per visit).

All changes are **uncommitted**. Dev server running on :5173.

One test limitation: signed-in persistence couldn't be exercised (no real credentials in preview) — but the Supabase layer degrades to local mode gracefully, so the app works either way.

Next natural steps:

Next natural steps: run the migration in Supabase so server-side persistence goes live; then optionally test a real email sign-up end-to-end to confirm the auth step hand-off and server resume.
