The logout data-isolation bug is fixed and verified live end-to-end.

## Root cause

The onboarding provider kept farm data under **global** localStorage keys (`krisiveda.onboarding.draft`, `.completed`). A signed-in user's `completeOnboarding` wrote their farm there, and the guest/anonymous tier read those same keys back — so after sign-out (especially via "Skip for now" guest mode), the previous user's 12-acre Basmati farm reappeared on My Farm, Cost & Profit, etc. Supabase queries were already user-scoped; only the local tier leaked.

## Changes (5 files)

- **`src/hooks/useAuth.jsx`** — `onAuthStateChange` now handles `SIGNED_OUT` explicitly: session nulls and the guest flag clears (signed-out ≠ guest). The Supabase session remains the single source of truth.
- **`src/hooks/useOnboarding.jsx`** — the core fix:
  - Signed-in users' drafts/completion flags now live under **user-scoped keys** (`...draft.<userId>`) that no other identity ever reads (§12/§13).
  - The signed-out and guest branches **hard-clear** all private state — memory + anonymous scratch keys — instead of reading them (§1/§2/§5).
  - One-time migration adopts a legacy global mirror into the owning user's scoped keys, then deletes the shared copy.
  - `completeOnboarding`/`skipOnboarding`/`saveDraft`/`resetOnboarding` write to the correct tier only.
- **`src/components/onboarding/EmptyFarmNotice.jsx`** — new signed-out branch: **"Sign in to view your farm details."** with the Sign In CTA → `/login`; authenticated-incomplete users keep the "Complete your farm details…" + wizard CTA (§7/§8).
- **`src/data/translations.js`** — new `onboarding.empty.signInToView` key in all 5 languages (compile-verified: en/bn/hi/te/ta each exactly once).
- **`src/pages/Dashboard.jsx`** — greeting prefers the signed-in account's name over the shared localStorage profile name (no previous-user name after logout).

## Verified live (preview walk)

| Scenario | Result |
|---|---|
| Guest with seeded previous-user farm data | Scratch keys wiped; "Sign in to view your farm details."; zero farm data |
| Anonymous (no session) | Redirected to `/login`; nothing leaked |
| User A signs in | Farm renders from A's scoped keys (12 acre / Traditional Basmati / Transplanting); legacy key migrated |
| **Sign out via UI** | Session cleared → `/login`, no guest flag, **no farm stats anywhere**, A's scoped keys preserved (not deleted, §6) |
| User B signs in on same device | Sees only B's farm (5 hectare / Gotra Bashi / Flowering) — A's data never rendered |
| User A logs back in | 12-acre farm fully restored (§17) |
| Sign out → "Skip for now" (the exact reported bug path) | Empty sign-in state, no 12-acre data (§16) |

Build ✓ (0.9s), lint ✓ (baseline 20 warnings / 0 errors, none in touched files). RLS policies in `supabase/migration_onboarding.sql` untouched, no Supabase rows deleted on logout, no UI redesign. The migration SQL still needs to be run in the Supabase SQL Editor (until then, persistence is local-tier only, as before).

Follow-ups worth considering:

One caveat: the forged-token test verifies the client pipeline, not real Supabase round-trips — worth a manual pass with a real account once the migration is applied.
