## Root cause

`.obw-rows` (the container holding the per-parcel rows) had `max-height: 44vh; overflow-y: auto` — added long ago so 20-parcel farms would scroll. Any overflow container **clips its descendants**, so the dropdown was cut off at the container's edge no matter what `z-index` it had. With 1 parcel the rows didn't even overflow, but the clipping box existed regardless, and the dropdown (which opens *below* the input) extended past it — forcing a scroll inside the form to see recommendations. The glass card itself was never the clipper (no `overflow: hidden` there), and z-index alone could never fix clipping.

## The three-line fix

1. **`.obw-rows`** — removed `max-height: 44vh; overflow-y: auto`, set `overflow: visible` (with a comment explaining why it must never regress). Very large parcel counts now grow the card, and `.auth-panel` already page-scrolls instead of clipping (its own documented behavior) — so nothing else needed to scroll.
2. **`.obw-variety__list`** — `z-index: 30 → 60`, comfortably above every sibling layer within the glass card (the card's `backdrop-filter` context already paints over the page background; the list only needed to win *within* the card).
3. **`.obw-variety__list`** — `max-height: min(240px, 34vh)`: on short 9:16 screens the open list now stays inside the viewport instead of poking past the screen edge; extra options scroll *inside the list* (its own internal scroll, per your requirement 13), never the form.

Requirements already satisfied by the existing design, left untouched: opaque `#101828` background (requirement 11 — never translucent), in-flow anchoring below the input (requirement 10/14 — stays glued when the mobile keyboard opens), ARIA combobox/listbox semantics, hover/active states, and all animations.

