Done and verified live with a screenshot. Two coordinated changes; everything else untouched.

## What changed

**`OnboardingWizard.jsx` — `VarietyInput` (the only component touched)**
1. **Removed the 8-result display cap** — `fuzzyRank(VARIETY_ENTRIES, value, VARIETY_ENTRIES.length)`. The old limit meant "a" could never show more than 8 options no matter how tall the dropdown got; ranking/filtering logic itself is untouched.
2. **Dynamic viewport-aware max height** — a small `useLayoutEffect` measures the space between the input's bottom and the **visible viewport** (`window.visualViewport`, so an open mobile keyboard is accounted for), minus a 10px breathing margin, clamped to `120px…480px`. It re-measures on open, window resize, and keyboard show/hide, and feeds the value to the list as an inline `maxHeight` (CSS alone can't know the distance to the screen edge).

**`OnboardingWizard.css`**
- The list's `max-height` becomes a `480px` pre-measure fallback (the inline style always overrides once measured) + `overscroll-behavior: contain` so an internal scroll at the screen edge can't chain into the page. Background, radius, typography, scrollbar, shadow, and the `z-index: 60` layering fix are all unchanged.

## Verified behavior (360×640 → 9:16-class mobile viewport, real input)

| Scenario | Result |
|---|---|
| Few matches ("pusa" → 3) | ✓ height = content (119px ≈ 117px), no empty space, no scroll |
