Fixed with a two-property CSS change in [Header.css](src/components/layout/Header.css#L570-L581) — no pixel offsets, no margins, pure flex:

```css
.profile-modal__confirm-actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;      /* vertical alignment of both buttons */
  justify-content: center;  /* row centered in the dialog */
  gap: 10px;
}

.profile-modal__confirm-actions .profile-modal__pill {
  flex: 1 1 0;
  justify-content: center;  /* label centered inside each pill */
}
```

**Root cause:** the row was already flex, but the pills only had `flex: 1 1 0` with no content justification — Cancel's short label hugged the left edge of its stretched pill while Sign Out (icon + text) nearly filled its own, which read as misalignment.

**Measured verification (DOM geometry, before → after):**

| Metric | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Row `align-items` / pills `justify-content` | `normal` | `center` / `center` |
| Button heights (Cancel vs Sign Out) | 32.3 / 32.3 px | 32.3 / 32.3 px — equal |
| Vertical centers | already equal | equal (same center line) |
| Cancel text off button center | — | **0.0 px** |
| Sign Out icon/text on same line + group centered | — | ✓ (icon, text, button all at 509.3px) |

Mobile at 375px: dialog 304px, both buttons within viewport, equal height, same center line, text centered. Widths, colors, borders, radius, icons unchanged; text, language system, logout logic, and modal positioning untouched.

