{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p18-7636c29f","text":"**Bug**: at 430px viewport, menu bottom = 440.5 > 430 — sticks 10.5px below the viewport! Why didn't place() constrain it?

place() logic:
```js
if (vh - b.bottom - GAP >= h) top = b.bottom + GAP;       // below
else if (b.top - GAP >= h) top = b.top - GAP - h;         // above
else top = Math.max(GAP, Math.min(b.bottom + GAP, vh - h - GAP));
```
vh=430, b.bottom=479.5?? Wait — the RAW btn rect I just measured: btn.t=448.5, b=479.5 — but menu placed at top 262.5 = 262.5 = ... b.top(448.5) − 8 − h(178) = 262.5 ✓ — it took the ABOVE branch: b.top − GAP = 440.5 ≥ h(178) ✓ → flipped above → bottom = 440.5, which is within... 440.5 ≤ 430? NO — 440.5 > 430. Wait the flip branch requires b.top − GAP ≥ h: 448.5 − 8 = 440.5 ≥ 178 ✓ — that checks the menu TOP is ≥ GAP... no wait: top = b.top − GAP − h = 262.5 ≥ 0 ✓. Menu bottom = b.top − GAP = 440.5. For bottom ≤ vh we need b.top − 8 ≤ vh → 479.5 ≤ 430 FALSE — btn is BELOW the viewport bottom edge?? btn bottom 479.5 > vh 430!

The button itself is below the fold — at 430px height, the popup content (hero 331px + info + prefs) doesn't fit; prefs row sits at y≈448-479, i.e., outside the visible viewport, only reachable by scrolling the internal scroll container. So the menu (correctly flipped above the button) also ends up mostly outside the viewport — because the ANCHOR is off-viewport!

This is the real-world case the user describes: on small screens the Language button may be scrolled out of view; the menu must remain fully visible. My placement must also clamp when the anchor itself is off-viewport: if the button is below the fold, opening "above" it still lands outside. Need: clamp top into [GAP, vh − h − GAP] regardless of branch — i.e., after computing the branch top, clamp:

```js
let top;
if (roomBelow) top = b.bottom + GAP;
else if (roomAbove) top = b.top - GAP - h;
else top = b.bottom + GAP;
top = Math.max(GAP, Math.min(top, vh - h - GAP));
```
With btn below fold (b.bottom 479.5): roomBelow: 430−479.5−8 <0 no; roomAbove: b.top−8=440.5 ≥ 178 yes → top=262.5 → clamp: min(262.5, 430−178−8=244) → 244 → menu at 244..422 — visible (button off-screen above it, but menu fully visible ✓). When the user scrolls the popup internally, rAF re-places → follows the button into view.

Also `internalScroll` check returned false because h=178 < available → after clamping, h still 178 (fit) → no internal scroll needed; the menu was just misplaced. The height-constrain (maxHeight) path only kicks in on REALLY short viewports (vh < 178+16). Fine.

But ALSO: menu must remain within viewport even when the anchor is far off-screen — with clamping it's always ✓.

One more consideration: when the anchor is entirely below the viewport, is showing the menu near the bottom edge useful? It's the spec's requirement ("constrain to viewport space") — yes, show it clamped; scrolling moves both into alignment.

