Language dropdown rebuilt as a proper floating menu, not another patch.

**The real bug** (found by comparing z-indexes live): the popup's top-level portal layer `.profile-modal__portal` sits at **z-index 9000**, while the portaled menu — despite being under `<body>` with `position: fixed` — was at **z-index 90**. They're body-level siblings, so the popup's layer buried the menu outright. No amount of overflow tweaking inside the popup would ever fix that; the menu needed to out-rank the popup layer.

**New architecture** — [LanguageMenu.jsx](src/components/layout/LanguageMenu.jsx), a self-contained portal component:
- Renders via `createPortal` under `<body>` as `position: fixed`, **z-index 9100** — fully independent of the popup's overflow, transform, filter, backdrop-filter and stacking contexts; verified by hit-test that the menu physically paints above the card
- Positions from the Language button's `getBoundingClientRect()`, measured before paint (opacity 0 until placed, no 0,0 flash), left-aligned, viewport-clamped
- Placement ladder: below the button → flip above (only when fully fitting) → constrain to viewport with internal scrolling; final clamp guarantees it's **always fully inside the viewport** even when the anchor itself has scrolled out
- Stays glued to the button: re-anchors every animation frame while open, plus resize + capture-phase scroll listeners
- Solid backgrounds (`#101712` dark / `#fffdf9` light), rounded, bordered, shadowed — a real floating menu

**Functional wiring** (no new language state): uses the existing `prefMenu`, `language`, `changeLanguage`; outside mousedown closes; **Escape closes just the menu** (capture phase, propagation stopped, so the popup doesn't close too); `closePanel` and popup unmount kill the menu so a reopened popup is always clean — all listeners and the rAF loop are torn down on close.

**Verified live**: all 5 options render immediately above the card (below the button with exact 8px gap at desktop); বাংলা click switches the app instantly and closes; active highlight follows the current language; outside-click, Escape, and popup-close each behave correctly; reopen is clean and the menu works again; mobile 375px and an extreme 430px-tall viewport both keep the menu fully visible (flip + clamp paths tested, including anchor-off-screen); light mode gives dark ink on warm white. Along the way the browser console caught a TDZ crash I'd introduced (`prefMenu` referenced before init in the popup's Escape effect) — reverted that branch, since the menu's own handler already owns Escape. Build ✓, lint **18w/0e**, all 7 test keys purged.

