{"kind":"tool","id":"KfjMjOhWtW4","toolName":"str_replace","input":{"path":"src/components/auth/Auth.css","replacements":[{"oldString":"/* True glassmorphism: see-through white tint (never black),\n   medium frosted blur so the rice field stays recognizable\n   through the panel, thin glass border, soft diffused shadow\n   and a faint top-edge highlight for the premium glass read. */\n/* Frosted-glass card: the panel's transform now releases at rest\n   (fill-mode backwards), so this backdrop-filter actually renders —\n   the photo behind the card is genuinely blurred while everything\n   painted INSIDE the card stays perfectly sharp (backdrop-filter\n   never touches an element's own content). The inputs'/Google\n   button's blur sits inside this backdrop root and samples the\n   already-frosted card surface — control surfaces read slightly\n   deeper-frosted than the panel, which is the intended premium\n   layering. Tint stays low-alpha: image recognizable, softly muted.\n   Blur is deliberately LIGHTER than the inner controls' 20px — the\n   panel is a subtle frost, the fields are the strong frost. */\n.auth-card {\n    width: min(412px, 100%);\n    /* Solid near-black sign-in card — no frosted translucent fill */\n    background: var(--bg-surface);\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    border-radius: 26px;\n    padding: 34px 32px 30px;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n    box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(4, 8, 16, 0.38);\n}","newString":"/* True glassmorphism: see-through white tint (never black),\n   medium frosted blur so the rice field stays recognizable\n   through the panel, thin glass border, soft diffused shadow\n   and a faint top-edge highlight for the premium glass read. */\n.auth-card {\n    width: min(412px, 100%);\n    /* Translucent dark glass over the agricultural slideshow — the\n       photo stays clearly recognizable through the panel, read as a\n       premium frosted surface, never a solid opaque rectangle. */\n    background: rgba(8, 9, 10, 0